WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.034
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.369
we're here with
Tracee Ellis Ross.

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.905
I do ask this question often of
people who figure --

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.774
or I should say finish long runs
on beloved shows --

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.544
did you,
I don't want to say stole,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:15.181
did you liberate anything
from the set?

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:19.852
-Yeah, I, um I asked to liberate
a piece of art

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.854
that had been on the wall,
it has not made it to me.

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:25.424
I am still under the hopeful
idea that it will show up

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.959
at my door in a package.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:29.161
I don't think I got
the piece of art I wanted.

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:32.131
I did, however, take as much
wardrobe as I possibly

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.600
could fit in my car.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.002
because Bow Johnson
had a great wardrobe.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:39.905
And at one point I was, like,
loading the back of my car

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:42.375
and an ABC executive walked by
and I was like,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.178
"Either turn around
or know that I am helping

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.413
the wardrobe department
and I'm bringing

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.249
these things to the cleaners.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.150
They are -- the cleaners is on
the way home

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.553
and I just want to help them out
to get all this stuff cleaned up

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:57.056
so you can pack it up.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.925
That was very, very kind.
You're a, you know,

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.526
you're a very charitable person.
-Awful.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.027
I'm sure he bought that,
hook, line, and sinker.

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:04.597
-Absolutely. And you know what,
everybody knows that about me.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.099
I'm helpful.
-Very helpful.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:10.069
Now, this is a time to embark on
new experiences,

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.404
when you wrap something like
this up.

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:17.176
I've heard tell that the next
frontier for you might be

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:20.779
trying stand up out,
is this true?

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:23.115
-It's a hope, it's a dream,
it's a wish.

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:27.786
I don't, I think -- okay --
it's clearly so much harder

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:31.324
than the greats, you know who
I'm looking at, Seth,

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:35.294
than y'all make it seem.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:38.497
-But I'm looking for
a tight five.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.066
-Alright. Well now --
-Isn't that the term?

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.235
Is that the term?
-Tight five, yeah.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.470
Is you can get a tight five
you're on your way.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.638
-Oh, okay.
All of a sudden it sounded

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:49.775
like I said something sexual.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.544
-Or, like, what I'm supposed to
achieve at the end of my diet.

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:54.514
Like a tight five.
-There's a different kind --

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.483
there's a different of, like,
people that will

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.186
will want a different kind of
tight five.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.222
Just steer clear of it.
-Okay. Right. Okay.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:05.391
So we don't want -- so will you
tell me what the top three

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.127
things are that I should think
about with stand up?

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.062
-Oh, that's a very --
that's a good question.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:13.399
I mean, it has to be things you
enjoy

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.568
that brings you joy
to say them out loud.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.702
-Okay.
-Like, I think that people

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.538
can tell when you're not joyous
about it.

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:20.973
-That's a good note.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:24.576
-I think that in your head,
your tight five is probably,

00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:28.014
at first writing, gonna be 10 or
15 minutes, right?

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.649
Like, it will, you have to be --

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.184
-This is getting harder
by the minute.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.286
-Yes, but it'll,
like, you just have to be,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.587
you know, sort of ruthless
at the editing of it.

00:02:35.587 --> 00:02:39.993
-Okay.
-And lastly, uh...

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.229
I would just say they can smell
your fear.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.698
So, you know. Don't have it.
-Well it's gonna be --

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.466
It's gonna be
a stinky room, Seth.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.034
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:51.471
-Well, no you did something
harder than a tight five.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.172
-What?
-So I saw this photograph.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.875
You took, you managed to get
your entire family,

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.377
including your mother
Diana Ross, to wear

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:02.181
the same matching pajamas and
take this Christmas photo.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:05.217
I mean, this is -- when I look
at the amount of people here,

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.586
I cannot believe this was pulled
off, it's a beautiful photo.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:11.023
-Not only -- well, my sister
Rhonda is not in the photo.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:15.661
Not only was it pulled off,
but I during the holidays,

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.930
am in charge of food and photos.
-Okay.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.066
-So I usually will cut --
I don't have children

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.301
so I have really strong
assignments.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:25.638
And this Christmas I was like
I'm not ruining this.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.607
I literally shipped my
Ring Light home.

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:31.076
So I shipped my Ring Light
and my tripod home.

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:34.047
We used to do family photos
where my mom would, like,

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:37.650
we would go to a costume shop,
and like, do Victorian costumes.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:42.755
But there's so many children and
so many husbands and wives now,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:47.894
we're like 22, that it's like
Amazon pajamas.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.528
And we got everyone in the
photo.

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:51.364
And my family, it's,
there's noth--

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.533
I just, I like and love
my family so much.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.302
And the holidays are, like,
our favorite time

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.537
to be holed up in the house
together.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:01.774
And, yeah, that photo's a good
capture of it.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.577
-I think the very wise thing you
did is, I noticed,

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:08.414
some of the younger people were
allowed to have bicycles?

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.650
-Yeah.
-That's very smart.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.785
In regard to keeping their
attention.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.988
Let 'em have the bikes.
-Well, let 'em have the bikes.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.357
Let 'em look at --
I mean, the whole beginning

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:21.060
of taking a photo is like,
"This way, this way, ha ha ha!

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.129
This way, this way. Look over
here. Look over --

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.231
Everlee look --
Everlee look over here."

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.665
You do that for, like,
10 minutes

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:28.133
and then you finally get
a photo.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.436
But my trick is I have a little
remote, in my hand.

00:04:31.436 --> 00:04:33.772
And I just snap and snap and
snap and snap and snap.

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:36.576
And then we have to go through,
like, 45 pictures.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:39.345
-Well, I -- let me just say that
there are 22 of you

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.215
and at least 15 of you are
looking at the camera.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:45.518
So great job.
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:46.953
-Hey, thanks for being here,
Tracee.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:50.756
Congratulations on eight seasons
and I do hope to see you soon.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.826
-Thank you so much, it's lovely
to see you as always.

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.461
-Tracee Ellis Ross, everybody.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.264
The final season of "Blackish"
airs Tuesday nights on ABC.

